#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Classify OpenRGB failures and perform narrowly reviewed latch recovery.

The status and prepare paths are read-only. Recovery is limited to explicitly
reviewed Tetris-only incidents or an exact stale lifecycle boundary, repeats
every applicable health gate, preserves the original evidence bytes, and
leaves the preference OFF. Lifecycle recovery may acknowledge the reviewed
boundary and start the user service exactly once; no path restarts a service,
starts a writer or effect, or selects a preset.

The administrative clearance paths are separately bound to source-reviewed
incidents. They perform no service operation; they only remove an unchanged
latch after two complete healthy-state reviews and protected evidence capture.
"""

